{% comment %}
  Step 5 (labeled "Step 4 of 5") — collects who the visit is for: full
  name, gender, phone number, and an optional email.

  MOBILE REDESIGN per a later Figma pass (node 438:7643), same instruction
  as the previous two steps: stay with the design, ignore backend
  integration.
  - Header swapped to the shared kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid
    snippet, and the appointment summary card is now the shared
    kal-booking-flow-appointment-card.liquid (same component Slot Picker
    uses) instead of no summary at all.
  - Top heading is now "Appointment Details" (matching the Figma page
    title), with "Who is this visit for?" moved to its own heading right
    above the form — previously that phrase was the ONLY heading, reused
    for both the mobile intro and the desktop left-column copy.
  - Phone Number field gained the Figma's country-code prefix (a
    decorative +91/India-flag chip, not a working country picker — same
    "visual match, not wired" treatment as the location badge's dropdown
    chevron elsewhere in this flow). Label text changed from "WhatsApp
    Number" to "Phone Number" to match the export; the underlying
    data-kal-field="whatsapp" identifier is untouched (JS validation
    keys off that, not the label).
  - Labels/inputs restyled to match the export (sentence-case medium-
    weight labels instead of bold uppercase eyebrow-style ones, #e5e1d9
    borders instead of #e6e6e8) — see kal-booking-flow.css's own comments.

  Gender is Male/Female only, not Male/Female/Other — explicit instruction,
  even though the Figma export showed three pill options (Female/Male/Other).
  patients.gender in the database accepts 'male'/'female'/'other', so this
  is a UI choice, not a backend constraint. Unchanged by this pass.

  NOT WIRED TO THE BACKEND YET (explicit instruction — "build the backend
  too but dont integrate it"). The backend already exists and needs no new
  code:
    1. POST /api/public/availability/holds { doctor_id, date, time } -> holdId
       (already called nowhere yet — would need to happen when a slot is
       picked, i.e. on the Slot Picker step's Continue, not here)
    2. POST /api/public/appointments { holdId, facilityId, doctorId,
       appointmentDate, appointmentTime, consultationMode, patientName,
       patientMobile, patientGender } -> books it and fires the WhatsApp
       confirmation
  This step's job when that's wired up: collect patientName/patientGender/
  patientMobile/patientEmail into slotPicker.patientDetails (see JS) so
  they're ready to send in step 2 above once the next step (booking
  confirmation) actually triggers it.

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — see the "SHARED
  STEP SHELL" comment in kal-booking-flow.css for why and how the layout
  switches at 750px. Every input/button below uses the same data-kal-field/
  data-kal-gender/data-kal-patient-continue hooks either way, so the JS
  validation and input-delegation logic in kal-booking-flow.js needs no
  changes to cover both sizes — it was already written expecting exactly
  this (see the comment above the `input` listener in that file). WhatsApp
  Number + Email are wrapped in .kal-form-row, which CSS stacks on mobile
  and puts side by side on desktop — the one genuine layout-only difference
  on this step.

  Left column / header pattern matches the other steps (chevron-left back
  button + progress dots, then eyebrow + heading via the same reused
  kal-step-doctor-select__intro classes as Slot Picker).
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-patient-details kal-step-shell">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__info-content">
      <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading">Who is this visit for?</h2>
      <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">
        Book a consultation in under a minute in-clinic or video. Confirmation
        arrives instantly, no account required.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-step-entry__location">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
        <!-- ICON: location-pin (not received yet) -->
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__location-text">
        Kerala Ayurveda Wellness Center, Indiranagar &middot; Opens 8 AM
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'slot-picker', step_number: 4, step_total: 5, next_label: 'Review & Payment' -%}

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
        <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Appointment Details</h2>
      </div>

      {%- assign appointment_photo_url = 'kal-doctor-photo-placeholder.jpg' | asset_url -%}
      {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-appointment-card', photo_url: appointment_photo_url, name: 'Dr. Neethu Jayachandran', price: '&#8377;500' -%}

      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
        <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Who is this visit for?</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-form">
        <div class="kal-form-field">
          <label class="kal-form-label" for="kal-patient-name">Full name*</label>
          <input
            type="text"
            id="kal-patient-name"
            class="kal-form-input"
            data-kal-field="name"
            placeholder="Enter full name"
            autocomplete="name"
          >
        </div>

        <div class="kal-form-field">
          <p class="kal-form-label">Gender*</p>
          <div class="kal-gender-group" data-kal-gender-group>
            <button type="button" class="kal-gender-btn" data-kal-gender="female">Female</button>
            <button type="button" class="kal-gender-btn" data-kal-gender="male">Male</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="kal-form-row">
          <div class="kal-form-field">
            <label class="kal-form-label" for="kal-patient-whatsapp">Phone Number*</label>
            {%- comment -%}
              Real, functional country-code picker — 9 countries, matching
              the CMS's own single source of truth for phone handling
              (app/lib/phone-validation.ts's COUNTRY_PHONE_OPTIONS) exactly,
              so this list and its digit-count rules don't drift from what
              the backend already validates. Replaces the earlier
              decorative +91-only chip; same look/position, now wired up.

              A native <select> can't render a flag graphic in its own
              closed state, so this is a custom button + listbox dropdown
              instead (explicit decision: keep the flag). Each option
              carries its dial code, min/max digit count, and an allowed-
              first-digit set as data attributes — data-kal-country-start
              flattens the CMS's MOBILE_START_DIGITS (which allows more
              than one starting pattern for some countries, e.g. Germany's
              "1" OR "567") into a single allowed-character set per
              country. That's a reasonable client-side approximation for
              this static picker, not a re-implementation of the full
              multi-pattern validator — the backend remains the real
              authority.

              The field's own identifier (data-kal-field="whatsapp") is
              unchanged, since JS validation keys off that.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="kal-phone-input">
              <div class="kal-country-picker" data-kal-country-picker>
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="kal-phone-input__country"
                  data-kal-country-toggle
                  aria-haspopup="listbox"
                  aria-expanded="false"
                >
                  <span class="kal-phone-input__flag" data-kal-country-flag>
                    {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-in' -%}
                  </span>
                  <span class="kal-phone-input__code" data-kal-country-code>+91</span>
                  <span class="kal-phone-input__chevron">
                    {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-down' -%}
                  </span>
                </button>
                <ul class="kal-country-picker__panel" data-kal-country-panel hidden role="listbox" aria-label="Country code">
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <button type="button" class="kal-country-picker__option" data-kal-country-option data-kal-country-iso="IN" data-kal-country-dial="+91" data-kal-country-min="10" data-kal-country-max="10" data-kal-country-start="6789" role="option" aria-selected="true">
                      <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-in' -%}</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__label">India</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__dial">+91</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <button type="button" class="kal-country-picker__option" data-kal-country-option data-kal-country-iso="US" data-kal-country-dial="+1" data-kal-country-min="10" data-kal-country-max="10" data-kal-country-start="" role="option" aria-selected="false">
                      <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-us' -%}</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__label">United States</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__dial">+1</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <button type="button" class="kal-country-picker__option" data-kal-country-option data-kal-country-iso="GB" data-kal-country-dial="+44" data-kal-country-min="10" data-kal-country-max="10" data-kal-country-start="7" role="option" aria-selected="false">
                      <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-gb' -%}</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__label">United Kingdom</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__dial">+44</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <button type="button" class="kal-country-picker__option" data-kal-country-option data-kal-country-iso="AE" data-kal-country-dial="+971" data-kal-country-min="9" data-kal-country-max="9" data-kal-country-start="5" role="option" aria-selected="false">
                      <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-ae' -%}</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__label">United Arab Emirates</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__dial">+971</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <button type="button" class="kal-country-picker__option" data-kal-country-option data-kal-country-iso="SG" data-kal-country-dial="+65" data-kal-country-min="8" data-kal-country-max="8" data-kal-country-start="89" role="option" aria-selected="false">
                      <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-sg' -%}</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__label">Singapore</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__dial">+65</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <button type="button" class="kal-country-picker__option" data-kal-country-option data-kal-country-iso="MY" data-kal-country-dial="+60" data-kal-country-min="9" data-kal-country-max="10" data-kal-country-start="1" role="option" aria-selected="false">
                      <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-my' -%}</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__label">Malaysia</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__dial">+60</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <button type="button" class="kal-country-picker__option" data-kal-country-option data-kal-country-iso="AU" data-kal-country-dial="+61" data-kal-country-min="9" data-kal-country-max="9" data-kal-country-start="4" role="option" aria-selected="false">
                      <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-au' -%}</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__label">Australia</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__dial">+61</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <button type="button" class="kal-country-picker__option" data-kal-country-option data-kal-country-iso="DE" data-kal-country-dial="+49" data-kal-country-min="10" data-kal-country-max="11" data-kal-country-start="1567" role="option" aria-selected="false">
                      <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-de' -%}</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__label">Germany</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__dial">+49</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                  <li role="presentation">
                    <button type="button" class="kal-country-picker__option" data-kal-country-option data-kal-country-iso="JP" data-kal-country-dial="+81" data-kal-country-min="10" data-kal-country-max="10" data-kal-country-start="0789" role="option" aria-selected="false">
                      <span class="kal-phone-input__flag">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'flag-jp' -%}</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__label">Japan</span>
                      <span class="kal-country-picker__dial">+81</span>
                    </button>
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <input
                type="tel"
                id="kal-patient-whatsapp"
                class="kal-form-input kal-phone-input__field"
                data-kal-field="whatsapp"
                placeholder="10-digit mobile number"
                autocomplete="tel"
                inputmode="numeric"
              >
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="kal-form-field">
            <label class="kal-form-label" for="kal-patient-email">
              Email <span class="kal-form-label__optional">Optional</span>
            </label>
            <input
              type="email"
              id="kal-patient-email"
              class="kal-form-input"
              data-kal-field="email"
              placeholder="Enter email address"
              autocomplete="email"
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="confirmation" data-kal-patient-continue disabled>
        Continue
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
